---
title: Accessibility
description: Give charts useful names, keyboard-equivalent interaction, reduced motion, redundant encodings, and exact-value alternatives.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessibility is part of the chart contract, not a final annotation pass.\nTanStack Charts provides named SVG and Canvas surfaces plus shared focus\nprimitives; the application still owns the surrounding explanation, controls,\nand exact-value alternative."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"name-the-chart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Name the chart"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every DOM host and framework adapter requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaLabel"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads for three packages\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaDescription"},{"type":"text","value":" when the reader needs context that is not already\nvisible nearby:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads for three packages\"\n  ariaDescription=\"Values are seven-day totals. Missing weeks are rendered as gaps.\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SVG renderer emits an image role, a chart roledescription, and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<desc>"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen a description is supplied. The Canvas renderer places the same image role,\nname, roledescription, description, and tab index on its root while keeping all\nfive canvas descendants "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not put instructions, conclusions,\nand all underlying data into one enormous accessible name."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"preserve-semantic-context-outside-the-surface","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preserve semantic context outside the surface"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A chart should usually be accompanied by:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a visible heading;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a short statement of what is being compared;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"units and time range;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a source note when relevant;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a summary or table when exact values matter."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use normal HTML for this content. It is easier to navigate, select, translate,\nand print than text embedded in SVG."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keyboard-focus-and-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyboard focus and selection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart-owned focus supports pointer and keyboard navigation over chart points.\nLeave "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard"},{"type":"text","value":" enabled when a chart is interactive. Focus callbacks expose\nthe same typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":" data regardless of input method."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the application replaces chart-owned focus with a brush, zoom, editor, or rich\noverlay:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provide semantic buttons, sliders, inputs, or table rows;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"keep visible focus styles;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"expose current state in text;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"support Escape when an interaction can be cancelled;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use live announcements sparingly for meaningful committed changes;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"make touch targets at least 44 CSS pixels where practical."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./interactions-and-selections.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactions and Selections"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide\ndefines the ownership boundary."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interactiveColorLegend"},{"type":"text","value":" uses native browser buttons with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-pressed"},{"type":"text","value":", a\nnamed group, 44-pixel minimum targets, and stable focus across controlled\nupdates. Static SVG output keeps only a visual fallback, so pair exported\ncharts with text or a table when series visibility must remain actionable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"brushX"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes its ordered handles as horizontal sliders when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" is\nprovided. Arrow keys move one authored value, Home and End move to the allowed\nrange edge, and Escape restores the range from the active pointer gesture.\nGive both handles distinct names and format their semantic values. The DOM\noverlay works with SVG and Canvas hosts; static SVG and React Native need an\napplication-owned range input for equivalent operation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continuousCursor"},{"type":"text","value":" paints an unsnapped pointer guide but does not expose that\npresentation-only overlay as a keyboard task. Pair its controlled x/y position\nwith named sliders or inputs and visible status text. Escape clears a visible\ncursor through the behavior; the semantic controls should update the same\ncontrolled position. Static SVG and React Native retain accepted guide paint\nbut still need those application-owned controls for operation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleX"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes one named horizontal slider. Left or Down moves to the\nprevious authored value, Right or Up moves to the next, and Home and End move\nto the candidate endpoints. Its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":" result becomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-valuetext"},{"type":"text","value":"; the\npointer target is 44 pixels high by default. Escape restores the gesture\norigin while a pointer or touch drag is active. Static SVG and React Native\nretain the accepted handle paint but need an application-owned semantic input."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"zoomX"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes one named plot surface with visible focus. Plus and minus zoom,\nthe arrow keys pan, Home resets, and Escape cancels an active gesture. Wheel\ninput is captured only while that surface is focused by default. For scrolling\ndashboards, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wheelActivation: 'modifier'"},{"type":"text","value":" lets Control+wheel or Command+wheel\nact immediately under the pointer while every unmodified wheel keeps scrolling\nthe page. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wheelActivation: 'always'"},{"type":"text","value":" deliberately captures every wheel over\nthe plot. Keep a visible Reset button and current-window text bound to the same\ncontrolled window. Static SVG and React Native render the accepted window but\nneed application-owned semantic zoom controls."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"never-rely-on-color-alone","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never rely on color alone"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pair semantic color with at least one other signal:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"direct labels;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"shape or stroke pattern;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ordering;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"position;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"text in a legend or linked table;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selected outlines and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-pressed"},{"type":"text","value":" state."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check contrast against the actual application background in both light and\ndark modes. The theme cannot infer whether an arbitrary data color is\naccessible."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"motion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default SVG tween and optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" renderer respect\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefers-reduced-motion"},{"type":"text","value":" by default. Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"respectReducedMotion: true"},{"type":"text","value":" unless\nan application has a stronger accessible motion policy. Reduced motion snaps\nentrance, update, and focus-state changes to final geometry without scheduling\nanimation frames."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion should explain continuity between states. It should not:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"delay access to current values;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"loop without a pause control;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"move the focus target away from keyboard users;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"encode the only evidence of a change."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./dynamic-data-and-animation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Data and Animation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the\nlightweight tween and optional spring renderer boundaries."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltips-are-supplemental","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltips are supplemental"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The built-in tooltip exposes its structured rows through a polite status region.\nIt is not a replacement for a label, axis, legend, or data table. Essential\ninformation must remain available without hovering."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For complex framework content, use the adapter's tooltip-body composition\nsurface. Its transient body is inert, so a display-only nested chart can remain\nvisible but does not enter the focus or accessibility order. Render controls\nonly while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":" is true. The pinned surface has non-modal dialog semantics,\nEscape and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dismiss()"},{"type":"text","value":" close it, and focus returns to the chart when dismissal\nstarts inside the body. Controls still need an intentional tab order and\naccessible names."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip.visibility: 'pinned'"},{"type":"text","value":" when no transient surface should be\nannounced. Focus and pinned mark styling remain available, while the tooltip\nelement and framework body mount only after activation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"linked-table-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linked table pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For analytical and operational charts, a linked table gives readers exact\nvalues and a familiar navigation surface. Selection state should be shared\nsemantically, rather than inferred from DOM nodes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyedSelection"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" for chart activation and selected\ngeometry. Keep the semantic HTML table, status announcement, and clear control\nin the application, bound to the same controlled selected key."}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"linked-chart-table-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"linked-chart-table","data-collapsed-indexes":"[2]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"environment\":\"charts-react\",\"files\":{\"/src/App.tsx\":\"import { useMemo, useState } from 'react'\\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\\nimport { createDefinition } from './chart'\\nimport { rows } from './data'\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null)\\n  const definition = useMemo(\\n    () => createDefinition(selectedId, setSelectedId),\\n    [selectedId],\\n  )\\n\\n  const selected = rows.find((row) => row.id === selectedId)\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section>\\n      <Chart\\n        definition={definition}\\n        height={280}\\n        ariaLabel=\\\"Customer onboarding observations\\\"\\n        ariaDescription=\\\"Select a point or a table row to inspect the same observation.\\\"\\n      />\\n      <div>\\n        <p role=\\\"status\\\" aria-live=\\\"polite\\\">\\n          {selected\\n            ? `${selected.product}: ${selected.setupMinutes} minutes, satisfaction ${selected.satisfaction}`\\n            : 'No observation selected'}\\n        </p>\\n        <button\\n          type=\\\"button\\\"\\n          disabled={!selected}\\n          onClick={() => setSelectedId(null)}\\n        >\\n          Clear selection\\n        </button>\\n      </div>\\n      <table style={{ width: '100%', borderCollapse: 'collapse' }}>\\n        <caption>Customer onboarding observations</caption>\\n        <thead>\\n          <tr>\\n            <th scope=\\\"col\\\">Product</th>\\n            <th scope=\\\"col\\\">Setup minutes</th>\\n            <th scope=\\\"col\\\">Satisfaction</th>\\n          </tr>\\n        </thead>\\n        <tbody>\\n          {rows.map((row) => {\\n            const isSelected = row.id === selectedId\\n            return (\\n              <tr key={row.id}>\\n                <th scope=\\\"row\\\">\\n                  <button\\n                    type=\\\"button\\\"\\n                    aria-pressed={isSelected}\\n                    onClick={() => setSelectedId(row.id)}\\n                    style={{\\n                      minHeight: 44,\\n                      fontWeight: isSelected ? 700 : undefined,\\n                    }}\\n                  >\\n                    {row.product}\\n                    {isSelected ? ' — selected' : ''}\\n                  </button>\\n                </th>\\n                <td>{row.setupMinutes}</td>\\n                <td>{row.satisfaction}</td>\\n              </tr>\\n            )\\n          })}\\n        </tbody>\\n      </table>\\n    </section>\\n  )\\n}\",\"/src/chart.ts\":\"import { defineChart, dot } from '@tanstack/charts'\\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\\nimport { controlledSignal } from '@tanstack/charts/interaction/signal'\\nimport { keyedSelection, whenSelected } from '@tanstack/charts/selection'\\nimport { rows, type Observation } from './data'\\n\\nexport function createDefinition(\\n  selectedId: string | null,\\n  onSelect: (id: string | null) => void,\\n) {\\n  const selection = keyedSelection<Observation, string, number, number>({\\n    selected: controlledSignal(selectedId, (next) => onSelect(next)),\\n    key: (datum) => datum.id,\\n  })\\n\\n  return defineChart({\\n    marks: [\\n      dot(rows, {\\n        id: 'observations',\\n        x: 'setupMinutes',\\n        y: 'satisfaction',\\n        key: 'id',\\n        r: 5,\\n      }),\\n      whenSelected(\\n        dot(rows, {\\n          id: 'selected-observation',\\n          x: 'setupMinutes',\\n          y: 'satisfaction',\\n          key: 'id',\\n          r: 8,\\n          strokeWidth: 3,\\n        }),\\n        selection,\\n      ),\\n    ],\\n    scales: {\\n      x: { scale: scaleLinear, axis: { label: 'Setup time (minutes)' } },\\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Satisfaction' } },\\n    },\\n\\n    selection,\\n  })\\n}\",\"/src/data.ts\":\"export interface Observation {\\n  id: string\\n  product: string\\n  setupMinutes: number\\n  satisfaction: number\\n}\\n\\nexport const rows: readonly Observation[] = [\\n  { id: 'atlas', product: 'Atlas', setupMinutes: 18, satisfaction: 9 },\\n  { id: 'beacon', product: 'Beacon', setupMinutes: 31, satisfaction: 7 },\\n  { id: 'comet', product: 'Comet', setupMinutes: 24, satisfaction: 8 },\\n  { id: 'delta', product: 'Delta', setupMinutes: 42, satisfaction: 6 },\\n  { id: 'ember', product: 'Ember', setupMinutes: 15, satisfaction: 10 },\\n]\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { useMemo, useState } from 'react'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { createDefinition } from './chart'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null)\n  const definition = useMemo(\n    () => createDefinition(selectedId, setSelectedId),\n    [selectedId],\n  )\n\n  const selected = rows.find((row) => row.id === selectedId)\n\n  return (\n    <section>\n      <Chart\n        definition={definition}\n        height={280}\n        ariaLabel=\"Customer onboarding observations\"\n        ariaDescription=\"Select a point or a table row to inspect the same observation.\"\n      />\n      <div>\n        <p role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n          {selected\n            ? `${selected.product}: ${selected.setupMinutes} minutes, satisfaction ${selected.satisfaction}`\n            : 'No observation selected'}\n        </p>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          disabled={!selected}\n          onClick={() => setSelectedId(null)}\n        >\n          Clear selection\n        </button>\n      </div>\n      <table style={{ width: '100%', borderCollapse: 'collapse' }}>\n        <caption>Customer onboarding observations</caption>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Product</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Setup minutes</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Satisfaction</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          {rows.map((row) => {\n            const isSelected = row.id === selectedId\n            return (\n              <tr key={row.id}>\n                <th scope=\"row\">\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    aria-pressed={isSelected}\n                    onClick={() => setSelectedId(row.id)}\n                    style={{\n                      minHeight: 44,\n                      fontWeight: isSelected ? 700 : undefined,\n                    }}\n                  >\n                    {row.product}\n                    {isSelected ? ' — selected' : ''}\n                  </button>\n                </th>\n                <td>{row.setupMinutes}</td>\n                <td>{row.satisfaction}</td>\n              </tr>\n            )\n          })}\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </section>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=linked-chart-table env=charts-react file=/src/App.tsx entry","title":"/src/App.tsx","file":"/src/App.tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart, dot } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { controlledSignal } from '@tanstack/charts/interaction/signal'\nimport { keyedSelection, whenSelected } from '@tanstack/charts/selection'\nimport { rows, type Observation } from './data'\n\nexport function createDefinition(\n  selectedId: string | null,\n  onSelect: (id: string | null) => void,\n) {\n  const selection = keyedSelection<Observation, string, number, number>({\n    selected: controlledSignal(selectedId, (next) => onSelect(next)),\n    key: (datum) => datum.id,\n  })\n\n  return defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      dot(rows, {\n        id: 'observations',\n        x: 'setupMinutes',\n        y: 'satisfaction',\n        key: 'id',\n        r: 5,\n      }),\n      whenSelected(\n        dot(rows, {\n          id: 'selected-observation',\n          x: 'setupMinutes',\n          y: 'satisfaction',\n          key: 'id',\n          r: 8,\n          strokeWidth: 3,\n        }),\n        selection,\n      ),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleLinear, axis: { label: 'Setup time (minutes)' } },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Satisfaction' } },\n    },\n\n    selection,\n  })\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"group=linked-chart-table file=/src/chart.ts","title":"/src/chart.ts","file":"/src/chart.ts"},{"type":"code","value":"export interface Observation {\n  id: string\n  product: string\n  setupMinutes: number\n  satisfaction: number\n}\n\nexport const rows: readonly Observation[] = [\n  { id: 'atlas', product: 'Atlas', setupMinutes: 18, satisfaction: 9 },\n  { id: 'beacon', product: 'Beacon', setupMinutes: 31, satisfaction: 7 },\n  { id: 'comet', product: 'Comet', setupMinutes: 24, satisfaction: 8 },\n  { id: 'delta', product: 'Delta', setupMinutes: 42, satisfaction: 6 },\n  { id: 'ember', product: 'Ember', setupMinutes: 15, satisfaction: 10 },\n]","lang":"ts","meta":"group=linked-chart-table file=/src/data.ts collapsed","title":"/src/data.ts","file":"/src/data.ts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/82-chart-table-selection/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open the full linked chart-and-table catalog case"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"testing-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Testing checklist"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test the finished application, not only the SVG or Canvas element:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigate the page and chart with a keyboard."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confirm visible focus and a logical navigation order."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Operate selection, pinning, zoom, and editing without a pointer."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify focus and selection persist correctly after data updates."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable reduced motion."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test light, dark, forced-colors, and increased text size."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inspect the accessible name and description."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confirm exact values are available outside hover-only UI."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confirm status and errors are not encoded only by color."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a screen reader on the complete task flow."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automated checks can catch missing names and invalid roles, but they cannot\ndecide whether the representation communicates the right thing."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"name-the-chart","text":"Name the chart","level":2},{"id":"preserve-semantic-context-outside-the-surface","text":"Preserve semantic context outside the surface","level":2},{"id":"keyboard-focus-and-selection","text":"Keyboard focus and selection","level":2},{"id":"never-rely-on-color-alone","text":"Never rely on color alone","level":2},{"id":"motion","text":"Motion","level":2},{"id":"tooltips-are-supplemental","text":"Tooltips are supplemental","level":2},{"id":"linked-table-pattern","text":"Linked table pattern","level":2},{"id":"testing-checklist","text":"Testing checklist","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nAccessibility is part of the chart contract, not a final annotation pass.\nTanStack Charts provides named SVG and Canvas surfaces plus shared focus\nprimitives; the application still owns the surrounding explanation, controls,\nand exact-value alternative.\n\n## Name the chart\n\nEvery DOM host and framework adapter requires `ariaLabel`:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads for three packages\"\n/>\n```\n\nUse `ariaDescription` when the reader needs context that is not already\nvisible nearby:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads for three packages\"\n  ariaDescription=\"Values are seven-day totals. Missing weeks are rendered as gaps.\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe SVG renderer emits an image role, a chart roledescription, and a `<desc>`\nwhen a description is supplied. The Canvas renderer places the same image role,\nname, roledescription, description, and tab index on its root while keeping all\nfive canvas descendants `aria-hidden`. Do not put instructions, conclusions,\nand all underlying data into one enormous accessible name.\n\n## Preserve semantic context outside the surface\n\nA chart should usually be accompanied by:\n\n- a visible heading;\n- a short statement of what is being compared;\n- units and time range;\n- a source note when relevant;\n- a summary or table when exact values matter.\n\nUse normal HTML for this content. It is easier to navigate, select, translate,\nand print than text embedded in SVG.\n\n## Keyboard focus and selection\n\nChart-owned focus supports pointer and keyboard navigation over chart points.\nLeave `keyboard` enabled when a chart is interactive. Focus callbacks expose\nthe same typed `ChartPoint` data regardless of input method.\n\nIf the application replaces chart-owned focus with a brush, zoom, editor, or rich\noverlay:\n\n- provide semantic buttons, sliders, inputs, or table rows;\n- keep visible focus styles;\n- expose current state in text;\n- support Escape when an interaction can be cancelled;\n- use live announcements sparingly for meaningful committed changes;\n- make touch targets at least 44 CSS pixels where practical.\n\nThe [Interactions and Selections](./interactions-and-selections.md) guide\ndefines the ownership boundary.\n\n`interactiveColorLegend` uses native browser buttons with `aria-pressed`, a\nnamed group, 44-pixel minimum targets, and stable focus across controlled\nupdates. Static SVG output keeps only a visual fallback, so pair exported\ncharts with text or a table when series visibility must remain actionable.\n\n`brushX` exposes its ordered handles as horizontal sliders when `values` is\nprovided. Arrow keys move one authored value, Home and End move to the allowed\nrange edge, and Escape restores the range from the active pointer gesture.\nGive both handles distinct names and format their semantic values. The DOM\noverlay works with SVG and Canvas hosts; static SVG and React Native need an\napplication-owned range input for equivalent operation.\n\n`continuousCursor` paints an unsnapped pointer guide but does not expose that\npresentation-only overlay as a keyboard task. Pair its controlled x/y position\nwith named sliders or inputs and visible status text. Escape clears a visible\ncursor through the behavior; the semantic controls should update the same\ncontrolled position. Static SVG and React Native retain accepted guide paint\nbut still need those application-owned controls for operation.\n\n`handleX` exposes one named horizontal slider. Left or Down moves to the\nprevious authored value, Right or Up moves to the next, and Home and End move\nto the candidate endpoints. Its `format` result becomes `aria-valuetext`; the\npointer target is 44 pixels high by default. Escape restores the gesture\norigin while a pointer or touch drag is active. Static SVG and React Native\nretain the accepted handle paint but need an application-owned semantic input.\n\n`zoomX` exposes one named plot surface with visible focus. Plus and minus zoom,\nthe arrow keys pan, Home resets, and Escape cancels an active gesture. Wheel\ninput is captured only while that surface is focused by default. For scrolling\ndashboards, `wheelActivation: 'modifier'` lets Control+wheel or Command+wheel\nact immediately under the pointer while every unmodified wheel keeps scrolling\nthe page. `wheelActivation: 'always'` deliberately captures every wheel over\nthe plot. Keep a visible Reset button and current-window text bound to the same\ncontrolled window. Static SVG and React Native render the accepted window but\nneed application-owned semantic zoom controls.\n\n## Never rely on color alone\n\nPair semantic color with at least one other signal:\n\n- direct labels;\n- shape or stroke pattern;\n- ordering;\n- position;\n- text in a legend or linked table;\n- selected outlines and `aria-pressed` state.\n\nCheck contrast against the actual application background in both light and\ndark modes. The theme cannot infer whether an arbitrary data color is\naccessible.\n\n## Motion\n\nThe default SVG tween and optional `motion()` renderer respect\n`prefers-reduced-motion` by default. Keep `respectReducedMotion: true` unless\nan application has a stronger accessible motion policy. Reduced motion snaps\nentrance, update, and focus-state changes to final geometry without scheduling\nanimation frames.\n\nMotion should explain continuity between states. It should not:\n\n- delay access to current values;\n- loop without a pause control;\n- move the focus target away from keyboard users;\n- encode the only evidence of a change.\n\nSee [Dynamic Data and Animation](./dynamic-data-and-animation.md) for the\nlightweight tween and optional spring renderer boundaries.\n\n## Tooltips are supplemental\n\nThe built-in tooltip exposes its structured rows through a polite status region.\nIt is not a replacement for a label, axis, legend, or data table. Essential\ninformation must remain available without hovering.\n\nFor complex framework content, use the adapter's tooltip-body composition\nsurface. Its transient body is inert, so a display-only nested chart can remain\nvisible but does not enter the focus or accessibility order. Render controls\nonly while `pinned` is true. The pinned surface has non-modal dialog semantics,\nEscape and `dismiss()` close it, and focus returns to the chart when dismissal\nstarts inside the body. Controls still need an intentional tab order and\naccessible names.\n\nUse `tooltip.visibility: 'pinned'` when no transient surface should be\nannounced. Focus and pinned mark styling remain available, while the tooltip\nelement and framework body mount only after activation.\n\n## Linked table pattern\n\nFor analytical and operational charts, a linked table gives readers exact\nvalues and a familiar navigation surface. Selection state should be shared\nsemantically, rather than inferred from DOM nodes.\n\nUse `keyedSelection` and `whenSelected` for chart activation and selected\ngeometry. Keep the semantic HTML table, status announcement, and clear control\nin the application, bound to the same controlled selected key.\n\n```tsx group=linked-chart-table env=charts-react file=/src/App.tsx entry\nimport { useMemo, useState } from 'react'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { createDefinition } from './chart'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null)\n  const definition = useMemo(\n    () => createDefinition(selectedId, setSelectedId),\n    [selectedId],\n  )\n\n  const selected = rows.find((row) => row.id === selectedId)\n\n  return (\n    <section>\n      <Chart\n        definition={definition}\n        height={280}\n        ariaLabel=\"Customer onboarding observations\"\n        ariaDescription=\"Select a point or a table row to inspect the same observation.\"\n      />\n      <div>\n        <p role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n          {selected\n            ? `${selected.product}: ${selected.setupMinutes} minutes, satisfaction ${selected.satisfaction}`\n            : 'No observation selected'}\n        </p>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          disabled={!selected}\n          onClick={() => setSelectedId(null)}\n        >\n          Clear selection\n        </button>\n      </div>\n      <table style={{ width: '100%', borderCollapse: 'collapse' }}>\n        <caption>Customer onboarding observations</caption>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Product</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Setup minutes</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Satisfaction</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          {rows.map((row) => {\n            const isSelected = row.id === selectedId\n            return (\n              <tr key={row.id}>\n                <th scope=\"row\">\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    aria-pressed={isSelected}\n                    onClick={() => setSelectedId(row.id)}\n                    style={{\n                      minHeight: 44,\n                      fontWeight: isSelected ? 700 : undefined,\n                    }}\n                  >\n                    {row.product}\n                    {isSelected ? ' — selected' : ''}\n                  </button>\n                </th>\n                <td>{row.setupMinutes}</td>\n                <td>{row.satisfaction}</td>\n              </tr>\n            )\n          })}\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=linked-chart-table file=/src/chart.ts\nimport { defineChart, dot } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { controlledSignal } from '@tanstack/charts/interaction/signal'\nimport { keyedSelection, whenSelected } from '@tanstack/charts/selection'\nimport { rows, type Observation } from './data'\n\nexport function createDefinition(\n  selectedId: string | null,\n  onSelect: (id: string | null) => void,\n) {\n  const selection = keyedSelection<Observation, string, number, number>({\n    selected: controlledSignal(selectedId, (next) => onSelect(next)),\n    key: (datum) => datum.id,\n  })\n\n  return defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      dot(rows, {\n        id: 'observations',\n        x: 'setupMinutes',\n        y: 'satisfaction',\n        key: 'id',\n        r: 5,\n      }),\n      whenSelected(\n        dot(rows, {\n          id: 'selected-observation',\n          x: 'setupMinutes',\n          y: 'satisfaction',\n          key: 'id',\n          r: 8,\n          strokeWidth: 3,\n        }),\n        selection,\n      ),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleLinear, axis: { label: 'Setup time (minutes)' } },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Satisfaction' } },\n    },\n\n    selection,\n  })\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=linked-chart-table file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport interface Observation {\n  id: string\n  product: string\n  setupMinutes: number\n  satisfaction: number\n}\n\nexport const rows: readonly Observation[] = [\n  { id: 'atlas', product: 'Atlas', setupMinutes: 18, satisfaction: 9 },\n  { id: 'beacon', product: 'Beacon', setupMinutes: 31, satisfaction: 7 },\n  { id: 'comet', product: 'Comet', setupMinutes: 24, satisfaction: 8 },\n  { id: 'delta', product: 'Delta', setupMinutes: 42, satisfaction: 6 },\n  { id: 'ember', product: 'Ember', setupMinutes: 15, satisfaction: 10 },\n]\n```\n\n[Open the full linked chart-and-table catalog case](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/82-chart-table-selection/).\n\n## Testing checklist\n\nTest the finished application, not only the SVG or Canvas element:\n\n1. Navigate the page and chart with a keyboard.\n2. Confirm visible focus and a logical navigation order.\n3. Operate selection, pinning, zoom, and editing without a pointer.\n4. Verify focus and selection persist correctly after data updates.\n5. Enable reduced motion.\n6. Test light, dark, forced-colors, and increased text size.\n7. Inspect the accessible name and description.\n8. Confirm exact values are available outside hover-only UI.\n9. Confirm status and errors are not encoded only by color.\n10. Use a screen reader on the complete task flow.\n\nAutomated checks can catch missing names and invalid roles, but they cannot\ndecide whether the representation communicates the right thing.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Accessibility\ndescription: Give charts useful names, keyboard-equivalent interaction, reduced motion, redundant encodings, and exact-value alternatives.\n---\n\nAccessibility is part of the chart contract, not a final annotation pass.\nTanStack Charts provides named SVG and Canvas surfaces plus shared focus\nprimitives; the application still owns the surrounding explanation, controls,\nand exact-value alternative.\n\n## Name the chart\n\nEvery DOM host and framework adapter requires `ariaLabel`:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads for three packages\"\n/>\n```\n\nUse `ariaDescription` when the reader needs context that is not already\nvisible nearby:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads for three packages\"\n  ariaDescription=\"Values are seven-day totals. Missing weeks are rendered as gaps.\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe SVG renderer emits an image role, a chart roledescription, and a `<desc>`\nwhen a description is supplied. The Canvas renderer places the same image role,\nname, roledescription, description, and tab index on its root while keeping all\nfive canvas descendants `aria-hidden`. Do not put instructions, conclusions,\nand all underlying data into one enormous accessible name.\n\n## Preserve semantic context outside the surface\n\nA chart should usually be accompanied by:\n\n- a visible heading;\n- a short statement of what is being compared;\n- units and time range;\n- a source note when relevant;\n- a summary or table when exact values matter.\n\nUse normal HTML for this content. It is easier to navigate, select, translate,\nand print than text embedded in SVG.\n\n## Keyboard focus and selection\n\nChart-owned focus supports pointer and keyboard navigation over chart points.\nLeave `keyboard` enabled when a chart is interactive. Focus callbacks expose\nthe same typed `ChartPoint` data regardless of input method.\n\nIf the application replaces chart-owned focus with a brush, zoom, editor, or rich\noverlay:\n\n- provide semantic buttons, sliders, inputs, or table rows;\n- keep visible focus styles;\n- expose current state in text;\n- support Escape when an interaction can be cancelled;\n- use live announcements sparingly for meaningful committed changes;\n- make touch targets at least 44 CSS pixels where practical.\n\nThe [Interactions and Selections](./interactions-and-selections.md) guide\ndefines the ownership boundary.\n\n`interactiveColorLegend` uses native browser buttons with `aria-pressed`, a\nnamed group, 44-pixel minimum targets, and stable focus across controlled\nupdates. Static SVG output keeps only a visual fallback, so pair exported\ncharts with text or a table when series visibility must remain actionable.\n\n`brushX` exposes its ordered handles as horizontal sliders when `values` is\nprovided. Arrow keys move one authored value, Home and End move to the allowed\nrange edge, and Escape restores the range from the active pointer gesture.\nGive both handles distinct names and format their semantic values. The DOM\noverlay works with SVG and Canvas hosts; static SVG and React Native need an\napplication-owned range input for equivalent operation.\n\n`continuousCursor` paints an unsnapped pointer guide but does not expose that\npresentation-only overlay as a keyboard task. Pair its controlled x/y position\nwith named sliders or inputs and visible status text. Escape clears a visible\ncursor through the behavior; the semantic controls should update the same\ncontrolled position. Static SVG and React Native retain accepted guide paint\nbut still need those application-owned controls for operation.\n\n`handleX` exposes one named horizontal slider. Left or Down moves to the\nprevious authored value, Right or Up moves to the next, and Home and End move\nto the candidate endpoints. Its `format` result becomes `aria-valuetext`; the\npointer target is 44 pixels high by default. Escape restores the gesture\norigin while a pointer or touch drag is active. Static SVG and React Native\nretain the accepted handle paint but need an application-owned semantic input.\n\n`zoomX` exposes one named plot surface with visible focus. Plus and minus zoom,\nthe arrow keys pan, Home resets, and Escape cancels an active gesture. Wheel\ninput is captured only while that surface is focused by default. For scrolling\ndashboards, `wheelActivation: 'modifier'` lets Control+wheel or Command+wheel\nact immediately under the pointer while every unmodified wheel keeps scrolling\nthe page. `wheelActivation: 'always'` deliberately captures every wheel over\nthe plot. Keep a visible Reset button and current-window text bound to the same\ncontrolled window. Static SVG and React Native render the accepted window but\nneed application-owned semantic zoom controls.\n\n## Never rely on color alone\n\nPair semantic color with at least one other signal:\n\n- direct labels;\n- shape or stroke pattern;\n- ordering;\n- position;\n- text in a legend or linked table;\n- selected outlines and `aria-pressed` state.\n\nCheck contrast against the actual application background in both light and\ndark modes. The theme cannot infer whether an arbitrary data color is\naccessible.\n\n## Motion\n\nThe default SVG tween and optional `motion()` renderer respect\n`prefers-reduced-motion` by default. Keep `respectReducedMotion: true` unless\nan application has a stronger accessible motion policy. Reduced motion snaps\nentrance, update, and focus-state changes to final geometry without scheduling\nanimation frames.\n\nMotion should explain continuity between states. It should not:\n\n- delay access to current values;\n- loop without a pause control;\n- move the focus target away from keyboard users;\n- encode the only evidence of a change.\n\nSee [Dynamic Data and Animation](./dynamic-data-and-animation.md) for the\nlightweight tween and optional spring renderer boundaries.\n\n## Tooltips are supplemental\n\nThe built-in tooltip exposes its structured rows through a polite status region.\nIt is not a replacement for a label, axis, legend, or data table. Essential\ninformation must remain available without hovering.\n\nFor complex framework content, use the adapter's tooltip-body composition\nsurface. Its transient body is inert, so a display-only nested chart can remain\nvisible but does not enter the focus or accessibility order. Render controls\nonly while `pinned` is true. The pinned surface has non-modal dialog semantics,\nEscape and `dismiss()` close it, and focus returns to the chart when dismissal\nstarts inside the body. Controls still need an intentional tab order and\naccessible names.\n\nUse `tooltip.visibility: 'pinned'` when no transient surface should be\nannounced. Focus and pinned mark styling remain available, while the tooltip\nelement and framework body mount only after activation.\n\n## Linked table pattern\n\nFor analytical and operational charts, a linked table gives readers exact\nvalues and a familiar navigation surface. Selection state should be shared\nsemantically, rather than inferred from DOM nodes.\n\nUse `keyedSelection` and `whenSelected` for chart activation and selected\ngeometry. Keep the semantic HTML table, status announcement, and clear control\nin the application, bound to the same controlled selected key.\n\n```tsx group=linked-chart-table env=charts-react file=/src/App.tsx entry\nimport { useMemo, useState } from 'react'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { createDefinition } from './chart'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null)\n  const definition = useMemo(\n    () => createDefinition(selectedId, setSelectedId),\n    [selectedId],\n  )\n\n  const selected = rows.find((row) => row.id === selectedId)\n\n  return (\n    <section>\n      <Chart\n        definition={definition}\n        height={280}\n        ariaLabel=\"Customer onboarding observations\"\n        ariaDescription=\"Select a point or a table row to inspect the same observation.\"\n      />\n      <div>\n        <p role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n          {selected\n            ? `${selected.product}: ${selected.setupMinutes} minutes, satisfaction ${selected.satisfaction}`\n            : 'No observation selected'}\n        </p>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          disabled={!selected}\n          onClick={() => setSelectedId(null)}\n        >\n          Clear selection\n        </button>\n      </div>\n      <table style={{ width: '100%', borderCollapse: 'collapse' }}>\n        <caption>Customer onboarding observations</caption>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Product</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Setup minutes</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Satisfaction</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          {rows.map((row) => {\n            const isSelected = row.id === selectedId\n            return (\n              <tr key={row.id}>\n                <th scope=\"row\">\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    aria-pressed={isSelected}\n                    onClick={() => setSelectedId(row.id)}\n                    style={{\n                      minHeight: 44,\n                      fontWeight: isSelected ? 700 : undefined,\n                    }}\n                  >\n                    {row.product}\n                    {isSelected ? ' — selected' : ''}\n                  </button>\n                </th>\n                <td>{row.setupMinutes}</td>\n                <td>{row.satisfaction}</td>\n              </tr>\n            )\n          })}\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=linked-chart-table file=/src/chart.ts\nimport { defineChart, dot } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { controlledSignal } from '@tanstack/charts/interaction/signal'\nimport { keyedSelection, whenSelected } from '@tanstack/charts/selection'\nimport { rows, type Observation } from './data'\n\nexport function createDefinition(\n  selectedId: string | null,\n  onSelect: (id: string | null) => void,\n) {\n  const selection = keyedSelection<Observation, string, number, number>({\n    selected: controlledSignal(selectedId, (next) => onSelect(next)),\n    key: (datum) => datum.id,\n  })\n\n  return defineChart({\n    marks: [\n      dot(rows, {\n        id: 'observations',\n        x: 'setupMinutes',\n        y: 'satisfaction',\n        key: 'id',\n        r: 5,\n      }),\n      whenSelected(\n        dot(rows, {\n          id: 'selected-observation',\n          x: 'setupMinutes',\n          y: 'satisfaction',\n          key: 'id',\n          r: 8,\n          strokeWidth: 3,\n        }),\n        selection,\n      ),\n    ],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleLinear, axis: { label: 'Setup time (minutes)' } },\n      y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Satisfaction' } },\n    },\n\n    selection,\n  })\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=linked-chart-table file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport interface Observation {\n  id: string\n  product: string\n  setupMinutes: number\n  satisfaction: number\n}\n\nexport const rows: readonly Observation[] = [\n  { id: 'atlas', product: 'Atlas', setupMinutes: 18, satisfaction: 9 },\n  { id: 'beacon', product: 'Beacon', setupMinutes: 31, satisfaction: 7 },\n  { id: 'comet', product: 'Comet', setupMinutes: 24, satisfaction: 8 },\n  { id: 'delta', product: 'Delta', setupMinutes: 42, satisfaction: 6 },\n  { id: 'ember', product: 'Ember', setupMinutes: 15, satisfaction: 10 },\n]\n```\n\n[Open the full linked chart-and-table catalog case](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/82-chart-table-selection/).\n\n## Testing checklist\n\nTest the finished application, not only the SVG or Canvas element:\n\n1. Navigate the page and chart with a keyboard.\n2. Confirm visible focus and a logical navigation order.\n3. Operate selection, pinning, zoom, and editing without a pointer.\n4. Verify focus and selection persist correctly after data updates.\n5. Enable reduced motion.\n6. Test light, dark, forced-colors, and increased text size.\n7. Inspect the accessible name and description.\n8. Confirm exact values are available outside hover-only UI.\n9. Confirm status and errors are not encoded only by color.\n10. Use a screen reader on the complete task flow.\n\nAutomated checks can catch missing names and invalid roles, but they cannot\ndecide whether the representation communicates the right thing.\n"}
